Waves wrapper image notices
===========================

This image is published by Waves (https://github.com/ranokay/waves) and
bundles or derives from the following components. Full license texts ship
under /licenses; the Debian base's own license texts are under
/usr/share/common-licenses.

- wrapper-v2 (https://github.com/glomatico/wrapper-v2), the wrapper service
  and decrypt listener, under the Unlicense. The commit it was built from is
  recorded in this image's org.opencontainers.image.revision label and in
  docs/wrapper-image.md of the Waves repository.
- Android system libraries from the Android Open Source Project (AOSP),
  Apache-2.0 / BSD-licensed, staged from wrapper-v2's
  vendor/android-system tree (linker64, bionic, and the AOSP libraries
  Apple's binaries link against).
- The Debian base image and its packages, each under its own license.

Proprietary Apple libraries
---------------------------

This image also contains 18 native libraries extracted from Apple's
com.apple.android.music package (version 3.6.0-beta, build 1109) at image
build time: libCoreFP.so, libandroidappmusic.so, libCoreFoundation.so and
their peers. They are not covered by any license granted to Waves and remain
Apple's property. They are included only so the wrapper can decrypt the
user's own Apple Music downloads on the user's machine. See
docs/wrapper-image.md for the distribution caveat this implies.
